BANKON — Licensing (by component)
=================================

Parsec Wallet — Copyright (c) 2026 BANKON.

BANKON licenses by component. Where a source file carries an SPDX header, that header is
authoritative; otherwise REUSE.toml maps every path in this repository
(https://reuse.software). The full licence texts are in LICENSES/.


1. CLIENT-FACING ENCRYPTION SOFTWARE  →  GNU GPLv3-or-later  (LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt)

   Code that generates keys, derives them from a seed or mnemonic, holds key material, or
   signs transactions — the software users trust with their secrets:

     src-tauri/src/bankon_vault/**   the vault: Argon2id, wrapped DEK, per-entry HKDF
     src-tauri/src/chain_*/**        the signing packs (Algorand, Solana, Arweave, BTC, LTC, EVM)
     src-tauri/src/pmvpn/**          client-facing privacy transport
     src/lib/pmvpn/**                src/views/pmvpn.ts
     src/lib/crypto.ts               src/lib/keystore.ts
     src/lib/algorand-hd/**
     src/lib/algorand/account.ts     src/lib/algorand/assets.ts
     src/lib/algorand/transactions.ts  src/lib/algorand/validate.ts
     src/lib/arweave/seed.ts         src/lib/arweave/derive-worker.ts
     src/lib/arweave/jwk.ts          src/lib/arweave/ans104.ts
     src/lib/arweave/signer.ts       src/lib/arweave/tx.ts
     src/lib/solana/seed.ts          src/lib/solana/module.ts
     src/lib/solana/transfer.ts      src/lib/solana/kit-signer.ts
     src/lib/bitcoin/account.ts      src/lib/litecoin/account.ts
     src/lib/nfd/signer.ts           src/lib/builder/isolation.ts
     src/lib/dex/pact.ts             src/lib/dex/tinyman-onchain.ts
     src/lib/permaweb/wallet/keys.ts   src/lib/permaweb/evm/vault-key.ts
     src/views/admin-keygen.ts       src/views/create-wallet.ts
     src/views/import-wallet.ts      src/views/connect-approve.ts

   Like GnuPG — the GPL implementation of OpenPGP/PGP — cryptographic software that holds a
   user's keys is kept copyleft so that every derivative stays free and auditable. Anyone who
   ships a modified Parsec must ship their source too.

   There is deliberately NO permissive alternative on this tier. A dual licence here would let
   any fork elect the permissive option and close the very code that touches your keys, which
   is the outcome this tier exists to prevent.


2. EVERYTHING ELSE BANKON WROTE IN THIS TREE  →  Apache-2.0  (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)

   The wallet shell, views, routing, chain descriptors, namespace adapters, x402, the permaweb
   read paths, diagnostics, documentation and assets. None of it mints a key, holds key
   material, or produces a signature; it calls the tier above and is handed a signature back.

   Apache-2.0 carries an explicit patent grant and is the permissive licence most readily
   consumed downstream, including by Apache- and Google-ecosystem projects.


3. SERVER-SIDE / BACKEND  →  MIT  (LICENSES/MIT.txt)

   Code that runs on a server rather than on the participant's machine, and never holds a
   private key or passphrase:

     bankon-names-process/**   marketplace-process/**
     scripts/spawn-bnr.mjs     scripts/spawn-bmr.mjs


USER SOVEREIGNTY
----------------
Neither license, nor BANKON itself, asserts any control over your machine. BANKON preserves
your right to OWN YOUR FILESYSTEM and to do to your filesystem anything you, as its owner,
deem appropriate — install, modify, copy, delete, inspect, relocate, or destroy any part of
this software or its data. Your keys, your device, your data, your rules. Parsec runs entirely
on infrastructure you control, takes no custody of your keys, and never phones home.

The GPLv3's copyleft constrains the *redistribution of modified encryption code* — you must
pass on the same freedoms. It does not constrain your private use, nor what you do to your
own filesystem.


THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
--------------------
Third-party material keeps its own licence and copyright, as recorded in REUSE.toml. The
designs and ideas borrowed from other projects, and the licence of each source, are recorded
in docs/security/provenance.md.

This repository began as a fork of Web3dGuy/tauri-workflow-template, Copyright (c) 2025
Web3dGuy, released under the MIT License (LICENSES/MIT.txt). Files still carrying that
template's content retain its copyright notice and licence, as recorded in REUSE.toml.

